# ─── Local-only artefacts — never committed, never uploaded to git. ────
#
# cache/    : TRACKED — the five parquet inputs, the 7 graphs_<name>
#             grid variants, hashes.json, and the Kaggle dataset metadata
#             are committed so a fresh clone can run verify_env.py and the
#             test suite without rebuilding (see the cache block below).
#             Also uploaded to Kaggle as the versioned `dmrgt-cache`
#             dataset — the variants sit in the cache root precisely so
#             the plain `kaggle datasets version -p cache` includes them.
# artifacts/: outputs downloaded from Kaggle runs (predictions, metrics,
#             checkpoints, MLflow runs). Stays local.

# ── Virtual environment (recreate locally with `python -m venv .venv`) ─
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version

# ── Data cache — TRACKED on purpose ───────────────────────────────────
# Un-ignored in Phase 3 so the cache travels with the code: prices,
# features, targets, graphs (dynamic), graphs_frozen (per-fold static),
# graphs_<name> (the 7 sensitivity-grid graphs), hashes.json, and
# dataset-metadata.json are all committed. The hash gate in train.py and
# tests/test_graph_grid.py's content pins verify them on checkout.
#
# Everything in cache/ is flat on purpose: `kaggle datasets version -p
# cache` defaults to --dir-mode skip, which SILENTLY drops subdirectories,
# so a graph_variants/ directory would upload as nothing at all.
#
# Only credentials and stray checksum sidecars stay out of git:
cache/.kaggle/
cache/*.sha256

# ── Artifacts downloaded from Kaggle runs (predictions, metrics) ──────
artifacts/*.parquet
artifacts/*.json
artifacts/*.csv
artifacts/*.log
artifacts/*.pt
artifacts/*.pth
artifacts/checkpoints/
artifacts/mlruns/
artifacts/mlflow.db

# ── Python ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
*.egg-info/
*.egg
dist/
build/
.Python
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ── Notebooks ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.ipynb_checkpoints/
profile_default/
ipython_config.py

# ── ML / data science extras ──────────────────────────────────────────
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.pkl
*.pickle

# ── Editors / IDEs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Kaggle code datasets (assembled by build scripts; the copied modules
#    duplicate the repo roots — only the dataset metadata is tracked)
kaggle/code/configs.yaml
kaggle/code/model.py
kaggle/code/paths.py
kaggle/code/splits.py
kaggle/code/train.py
kaggle/code_phase3/*
!kaggle/code_phase3/dataset-metadata.json

# ── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/

# ── S&P 100 data build: venv and large build outputs stay local ──
data_build/sp100/out_*/
data_build/sp100/dmrgt-sp100-cache/
data_build/sp100/build_*.log
